    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance that is visible from the road in both directions.\n• Keep the circular driveway clear of parked vehicles so responding units can pull through without backing out.\n• Mark or label the detached structure on any posted site map so arriving crews know a second building is on the property.\n• Post a site map near the driveway entrance showing the locations of the main residence, detached structure, and any utility shutoffs.\n• Trim vegetation along the driveway to maintain clear sightlines and overhead clearance for responding vehicles.\n• Create or maintain a pedestrian path connecting the main residence to the detached structure that is passable on foot at night.\n• Keep a gate or opening in the perimeter fencing at the rear of the property unlocked and accessible for emergency crews.\n• If rear access through the fencing requires a key or combination, provide that information to the local fire department."
